# SafeTube secrets template
# -------------------------
# The Secrets Gradle Plugin reads `.env` (and falls back to this `.env.example`
# file when `.env` is absent) and exposes the values as BuildConfig fields.
# The app builds and runs fine with the placeholders below — the YouTube
# player and search work without any API key (public endpoints are used).

# Copy this file to `.env` and paste your real keys if you have them:

# Google AI Studio (Gemini) API key
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# YouTube Data API v3 key (optional — used for richer trending/search data)
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=your_youtube_api_key_here

# Firebase App Check debug token (optional, ignored in release builds)
FIREBASE_APPCHECK_DEBUG_TOKEN=your_appcheck_debug_token_here
